 are used when applications are accessed only internally and do not require=
 public internet exposure. This matches the scenario where users are connec=
ting through VPNs, either point-to-site or site-to-site, and need internal =
routing of traffic to backend virtual machines hosting App1.<br></p><p><cod=
e><strong>an Azure Application Gateway</strong></code> is also <strong>corr=
ect</strong> because it is a layer-7 (application layer) load balancer that=
 can intelligently route traffic based on HTTP/HTTPS requests. It is suitab=
le for web applications like App1, providing features such as URL-based rou=
ting, SSL termination, and session affinity, ensuring optimized and secure =
delivery of requests to the virtual machines hosting App1.<br></p><p><code>=
<strong>a public load balancer</strong></code> is <strong>incorrect</strong=
> because it distributes incoming traffic from public IP addresses. In this=
 scenario, the application is accessed internally through VPN connections r=
ather than from the public internet.<br></p><p><code><strong>an Azure Conte=
